chorus:eventtype-deploy-allow-set-gate-passed a chorus:EventType ;
    rdfs:label "deploy.allow_set_gate.passed" ;
    chorus:eventName "deploy.allow_set_gate.passed" ;
    chorus:eventCategory "fact" ;
    chorus:producedBy chorus:deploys ;
    chorus:eventVersion "1" ;
    chorus:atVertebra "operations" ;
    chorus:emitterSource "werk-deploy" ;
    chorus:joinKeys "trace" ;
    rdfs:comment "#3785 — the allow-set gate ran before an identity-touching deploy committed, and the store resolved a non-empty set of principals. Exists because on 2026-08-06 the doors came up reading an empty allow-set and the only signal was a warning on stderr that nobody was reading; the symptom surfaced minutes later as a human being told he was not on the team list. A warning is not a gate. Scoped to deploys whose diff touches identity surfaces, so it does not fire on docs cards and teach people to ignore it." ;
    chorus:payloadField "detail: the gate's own line, including the principal count and the graph it resolved from" .

chorus:eventtype-deploy-allow-set-gate-refused a chorus:EventType ;
    rdfs:label "deploy.allow_set_gate.refused" ;
    chorus:eventName "deploy.allow_set_gate.refused" ;
    chorus:eventCategory "fact" ;
    chorus:producedBy chorus:deploys ;
    chorus:eventVersion "1" ;
    chorus:atVertebra "operations" ;
    chorus:emitterSource "werk-deploy" ;
    chorus:joinKeys "trace" ;
    rdfs:comment "#3785 — the allow-set gate REFUSED a deploy: the store resolved zero principals, or could not be asked at all. Both are refusals and the distinction is in the reason — could-not-ask is not the same as nobody-allowed, and neither is a safe deploy. Deploying either state would fail every door closed for everyone, including whoever would fix it. KNOWN GAP (#3788): non-zero is the wrong assertion. On 2026-08-07 the set held only three workers — non-empty, gate passed, and every human and agent was locked out of governed writes. The widened check asserts named presence, not a count." ;
    chorus:payloadField "reason: why it refused — zero principals, or the store did not answer" .

